message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Empty-State Observatory: browser guessing game and synthetic 32-state monitor benchmark"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/empty-state-observatory"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Empty-State Observatory is a browser-based, software-only guessing game and
  reproducible synthetic benchmark. A visitor watches two seeded evolutions of
  an abstract, initially empty 32-state ring, guesses which run received a
  hidden synthetic disturbance, then reveals, replays or exports it. The ring
  evolves by a stable explicit heat step on its graph Laplacian with seeded
  forcing and noise. An OES-32-inspired consistency monitor checks peak,
  antipodal and FOLD8 residuals against a time-aligned clean reference and is
  benchmarked against a scalar RMS baseline for false alarms, detection rate,
  delay and misses. Scope: all traces, disturbances, scores and benchmark
  results are SYNTHETIC. It is not a model of physical universe dynamics,
  cosmology, quantum coherence or hardware, and its thresholds are documented
  design parameters, not calibrated limits.
keywords:
  - research software
  - synthetic benchmark
  - graph Laplacian
  - anomaly detection
  - educational game
  - JavaScript
  - Python
  - New Brunswick
